    "_about": "THE IMPALA (2026-11-05, gen: scratchpad sc/new6/impala_base.py, the deer frame's cervid sculpt): a slender, leggy antelope of 0.9 m at the withers, the neck of moderate length carried at ~45 degrees -- three tones in level bands: a red-brown saddle over the back and upper flank, a fawn band along the lower flank, the belly white (the countershade's three levels); a white chin, lips and throat patch, a white brow over each eye; black-tipped ears; from behind a white rump between two black vertical stripes down the buttocks, a white tail with a black line along its top; black tufts on the back of the hind fetlocks; the ram's lyre-shaped horns -- up and back from the brow, out, then up and the points forward -- thick at the base and tapering hard, irregularly ringed for two thirds of their length (the `ridges` coat), smooth to the points, rooted on the skull above and behind the eyes (2026-11-08) The HORNS are the engine's sharp `horn` (sharp.js; tools/creaturegen/sharp/horns.py merged the field part and its slender detail tip into one centreline): smooth, sunk in the skull, a true point. (2026-11-08, ears2.py) The EARS (ears2.py): long pointed LEAVES (sharp.js `fin`), white in the hollow, the tips black; the roots faired.",
